{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 694 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D7"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the lorazepam injection shortage on 2018-05-03 and it remains Current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E35", "E31", "E32", "E33", "E34"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our 2 mg/mL, 1 mL cartridges at both Corvale sites carry NDC 00409198530, which labels Hospira, Inc. as the product labeler.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E5"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The registered plant for that label is Hospira, Inc. (FEI 1925262).",
      "cites": ["E18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 976095 at that plant ended 2016-06-08 and was classified OAI, 694 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D7", "E12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Warning Letter was issued to the same plant on 2017-02-14, 443 days before the posting.",
      "cites": ["D9", "E17"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later inspection 1064827 ended 2018-08-15 and was also classified OAI, 104 days after the posting.",
      "cites": ["D13", "E14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑ranked option is to transfer 4 units of 2 mg/mL, 1 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would raise East's supply from 3.4 to 4 days while General retains 14 days.",
      "cites": ["D17"]
    }
  ]
}
